{%- comment -%}
  Featured products — the "Most Loved" row. A display heading, a micro label
  and a link out, above a grid that reflows on available width.

  The row is either that grid — unchanged, and the default — or a carousel of
  the same cards. The carousel is **not in the design**: the design's own
  homepage lays Most Loved out as a grid and has no slider anywhere. What is
  the design's is every part of how this one moves, so it reads as the same
  maison rather than as a plugin dropped in:

    - "Slide" is the quick view gallery's motion — one track translated by
      whole pages, `transform 0.6s var(--ease)`.
    - "Fade" is the hero carousel's — the window of cards is swapped in place
      and each one replays `gj-card` (rise and fade, 0.5s) 80ms apart.
    - The arrows are the hero's `hero-carousel__below` controls: centred under
      the track, ink at 60% turning `--c-accent`, and gone entirely when there
      is nothing to cycle through (`.hero-carousel.is-static`'s rule).

  Nothing here is load-bearing without scripting. The track is the very same
  `.grid-auto grid-auto--products` element in both layouts, so a visitor with
  no JavaScript gets the grid — every card in it, every link real — and the
  controls, which would be a lie, never appear.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign collection = collections[section.settings.collection]

  comment
    How many pieces the row shows. Off by default the section shows the whole
    collection; `limit_products` is what brings the count setting into play,
    and the editor only offers that setting while it is on.

    Shopify caps an un-paginated `collection.products` loop at 50 whatever is
    asked for, so "all" means "up to 50" — the same ceiling the collection
    template lives with.

    The placeholder branch below still needs a number when there is no
    collection to count, so the setting's own value stands in there.
  endcomment
  assign limit = section.settings.products_to_show
  unless section.settings.limit_products
    if collection != blank
      assign limit = collection.all_products_count
    endif
  endunless

  assign is_carousel = false
  if section.settings.layout == 'carousel'
    assign is_carousel = true
  endif

  comment
    How many cards are actually rendered — and so, at one card per page, the
    most pages the carousel can ever have. The dots are rendered by Liquid
    like everything else and the script only hides the surplus.
  endcomment
  assign card_count = limit
  if collection.products.size > 0
    assign card_count = collection.products.size
    if card_count > limit
      assign card_count = limit
    endif
  endif

  assign carousel_label = section.settings.heading
  if carousel_label == blank
    assign carousel_label = 'general.carousel.label' | t
  endif

  assign view_all = section.settings.view_all_label
  if view_all == blank and collection != blank
    assign view_all = 'collections.view_all_count' | t: count: collection.all_products_count
  elsif view_all == blank
    assign view_all = 'collections.view_all' | t
  endif

  comment
    Where "View all" goes. The collection this section is showing, by default —
    it is the obvious destination and needs no setting to be right — with an
    override for the case where it is not, say a curated landing page or a
    filtered URL. All products stands in when no collection is chosen, so the
    link always has a real destination and never becomes an `href="#"`.
  endcomment
  assign view_all_url = section.settings.view_all_link
  if view_all_url == blank
    assign view_all_url = collection.url | default: routes.all_products_collection_url
  endif
-%}

<section
  class="section scheme-{{ section.settings.color_scheme }}{% if section.settings.full_height %} section--tall{% endif %}"
  style="{% render 'section-style', padding_top: section.settings.padding_top, padding_bottom: section.settings.padding_bottom %}"
>
  <div class="page-width">
    {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
      <div class="display reveal">{{ section.settings.heading }}</div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if section.settings.subheading != blank or section.settings.show_view_all -%}
      <div class="section-header reveal">
        {%- if section.settings.subheading != blank -%}
          <span class="micro">{{ section.settings.subheading }}</span>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if section.settings.show_view_all -%}
          <a class="link-rule" href="{{ view_all_url }}">
            {{ view_all }}&nbsp;&nbsp;&rarr;
          </a>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      The column floor is `.grid-auto--products`' own now, so both layouts and
      every other product grid read one rule. The carousel works out how many
      cards fit by measuring a hidden box carrying that same expression, so the
      two can never disagree about a column count.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- capture grid_vars -%}
      --gap: var(--grid-gap);
    {%- endcapture -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      The cards themselves are identical in both layouts. In the grid each one
      carries its own `.reveal` and the design's 60ms stagger; in the carousel
      the component reveals as a whole and the cards' entrance is `gj-card`,
      staggered by their place in the visible page — the hero's own idiom, and
      the one that has to be replayed on every change in fade mode.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- capture cards -%}
      {%- if collection.products.size > 0 -%}
        {%- for product in collection.products limit: limit -%}
          <div
            {% if is_carousel %}class="fp-carousel__cell" data-fp-cell{% else %}class="reveal" style="--reveal-delay: {{ forloop.index0 | times: 60 }}ms;"{% endif %}
          >
            {% render 'product-card', product: product %}
          </div>
        {%- endfor -%}
      {%- else -%}
        {%- for i in (1..limit) -%}
          <div
            {% if is_carousel %}class="fp-carousel__cell" data-fp-cell{% else %}class="reveal" style="--reveal-delay: {{ forloop.index0 | times: 60 }}ms;"{% endif %}
          >
            {% render 'product-card' %}
          </div>
        {%- endfor -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endcapture -%}

    {%- if is_carousel -%}
      <div
        class="fp-carousel reveal"
        data-fp-carousel
        data-fp-motion="{{ section.settings.carousel_motion }}"
        role="group"
        aria-roledescription="{{ 'general.carousel.role' | t }}"
        aria-label="{{ carousel_label | escape }}"
      >
        <div class="fp-carousel__viewport" data-fp-viewport>
          {%- comment -%}
            The ruler. It is never seen and never in the flow — it exists so
            the script can ask the browser how wide a column would be under
            `.grid-auto`'s rule instead of re-deriving that rule in JavaScript.
            Every threshold, the 440px single-column override included, stays
            in the stylesheet where the grid's own are.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="fp-carousel__track grid-auto grid-auto--products" data-fp-track style="{{ grid_vars | strip }}">
            <div class="fp-carousel__ruler" data-fp-ruler aria-hidden="true"></div>
            {{ cards }}
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="fp-carousel__controls" data-fp-controls hidden>
          <button
            class="fp-carousel__arrow"
            type="button"
            data-fp-step="-1"
            aria-label="{{ 'general.carousel.previous' | t }}"
          >
            &larr;
          </button>

          <div class="fp-carousel__dots" data-fp-dots>
            {%- for i in (1..card_count) -%}
              <button
                class="fp-carousel__dot"
                type="button"
                data-fp-dot="{{ forloop.index0 }}"
                aria-label="{{ 'general.carousel.go_to_page' | t: number: forloop.index }}"
                hidden
              ></button>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </div>

          <button
            class="fp-carousel__arrow"
            type="button"
            data-fp-step="1"
            aria-label="{{ 'general.carousel.next' | t }}"
          >
            &rarr;
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>
    {%- else -%}
      <div class="grid-auto grid-auto--products" style="{{ grid_vars | strip }}">
        {{ cards }}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:sections.featured_products.name",
  "tag": "div",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "color_scheme",
      "id": "color_scheme",
      "label": "t:sections.all.color_scheme.label",
      "default": "scheme_1"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "t:sections.all.heading.label",
      "default": "Most Loved"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "subheading",
      "label": "t:sections.all.subheading.label",
      "default": "Our most loved creations"
    },
    {
      "type": "collection",
      "id": "collection",
      "label": "t:sections.featured_products.collection.label"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "layout",
      "label": "t:sections.all.layout.label",
      "info": "t:sections.featured_products.layout.info",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "grid",
          "label": "t:sections.featured_products.layout.grid"
        },
        {
          "value": "carousel",
          "label": "t:sections.featured_products.layout.carousel"
        }
      ],
      "default": "grid"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "carousel_motion",
      "label": "t:sections.featured_products.carousel_motion.label",
      "info": "t:sections.featured_products.carousel_motion.info",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "slide",
          "label": "t:sections.featured_products.carousel_motion.slide"
        },
        {
          "value": "fade",
          "label": "t:sections.featured_products.carousel_motion.fade"
        }
      ],
      "default": "slide",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.layout == 'carousel' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "limit_products",
      "label": "t:sections.featured_products.limit_products.label",
      "info": "t:sections.featured_products.limit_products.info",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "products_to_show",
      "label": "t:sections.featured_products.products_to_show.label",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.limit_products }}",
      "min": 2,
      "max": 16,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 8
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_view_all",
      "label": "t:sections.featured_products.show_view_all.label",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "view_all_label",
      "label": "t:sections.featured_products.view_all_label.label",
      "info": "t:sections.featured_products.view_all_label.info"
    },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "view_all_link",
      "label": "t:sections.featured_products.view_all_link.label",
      "info": "t:sections.featured_products.view_all_link.info"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "full_height",
      "label": "t:sections.all.full_height.label",
      "default": false
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:sections.all.spacing_header"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_top",
      "label": "t:sections.all.padding_top.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 200,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 72
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_bottom",
      "label": "t:sections.all.padding_bottom.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 200,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 72
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "t:sections.featured_products.name"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
